<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    What the tool needs from the operating system, and nothing else: run an external process under a
    time budget, and delete a temporary directory without ever failing the run over it.

    It exists so that no assembly has to name another to share them. The core declares IChangeSource
    and must not know who implements it - and an InternalsVisibleTo naming an implementation is such
    knowledge, written into the core's own build. Adding a second source would have meant editing the
    core to name it too. Both sides reference this instead, and neither names the other.

    Public, deliberately. These are shared by assemblies rather than within one, which is what a
    public type is for; the alternative was to keep them internal and pay for it with that reference.
  -->

</Project>
